<p>Well the rock contains trillions of parallel instances of this universe (and as far as they know most atoms in all kinds of matter contain similar structures), and they've been dying one by one since the twenties through natural causes. This item has no interaction with occult stuff or property you wouldn't expect from any rock&#8230; My idea is that pretty much every quark contains a universe, so it was probable that at some point, one would develop <em>through completely natural means, just like life on Earth did</em>, a civilisation so advanced it managed to send a signal at our scale, but (but of course that implies acting <em>within its universe</em> without breaking the laws of physics by basically getting it to vibrate in a preset pattern, destroying all life within it in the process. They can't &quot;get outside&quot; any more than we can get outside our universe). And the Foundation has done <strong>decades</strong> of research since its discovery to confirm all of this. Nothing about that makes it a potential threat. And on top of that, the bulk of the message has already been recorded twice. So the case that that this item could be abandoned without consequences seems strong to me!</p>

